{
  "abstract": "At every sufficiently large order n, we construct a split graph with an integral–fractional clique-partition gap of order at least (pn)^(3/2). If p^2 n exceeds an explicit constant times log n, independent survival of crossing edges with probability p leaves, with probability at least 1 - 2 n^(-8), both a complete physical reassignment and the same gap. The accompanying bipartite lemma explicitly chooses each host from its own surviving list.",
